course: dictionary
lesson: 1394
title: Caracaras: walkers and scavengers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A caracara is a large bird of prey from the Americas. It is related to falcons, but it has long legs and often a bare red or orange face. Say it kar-ah-KAR-ah.
explain: Many birds of prey stay in the air or sit high in trees. A caracara often walks on the ground, and it eats dead animals as well as live prey. That makes it both a hunter and a scavenger.
explain: Look at this sentence: «Birds such as cattle tyrants and yellow-headed caracaras ride on capybaras and eat ticks and flies.» The caracara gets a meal, and the capybara gets rid of ticks and flies. Both gain, which scientists call mutualism.
fact: A caracara is a large bird of prey from the Americas.
fact: Caracaras are related to falcons, but they have longer legs.
fact: Many caracaras have a bare red or orange face.
fact: A caracara walks on the ground and eats dead animals as well as live prey.
fact: «Mutualism» means a relationship where both living things gain something.
exercise: What is a caracara? | A kind of plant with red flowers | A small fish that lives in rivers | *A large bird of prey from the Americas | A large mammal that lives in the desert
exercise: What does a caracara eat? | Only grass from the fields | *Dead animals as well as live prey | Only seeds and fruit | Only fish from the sea
exercise: In the sentence about yellow-headed caracaras, what does mutualism mean? | Neither animal is affected at all | Only one animal gains and the other loses | *Both living things gain from the relationship | Both animals fight each other
test: Which bird is caracara related to? | Penguins | Parrots | *Falcons | Owls
test: Which part of a caracara is often bare and red or orange? | Its tail feathers | *Its face | Its wings | Its feet
exam: Which statement about caracaras is true? | Caracaras never walk on the ground | Caracaras cannot hunt live prey | Caracaras only live in Africa | *Caracaras can walk on the ground and eat dead animals
